godot-patches/0017: a depth pre-pass for opaque cut-outs in the Mobile renderer.

`rendering/renderer/cutout_depth_prepass_mobile` (0 off, the default; 1 GREATER_OR_EQUAL; 2 EQUAL; read each
frame). An opaque-list surface whose shader declares `depth_prepass_alpha` and has a `discard` (and writes no
ALPHA) is drawn twice in the opaque pass: first, before the whole opaque list, with its shadow version
(MODE_RENDER_DEPTH: vertex stage, alpha fetch and discard; colour writes masked); then in the list's own order with
its colour version and no depth write, compare GREATER_OR_EQUAL (the discard keeps the holes) or EQUAL. A discard
without a depth write keeps the early depth test, so hidden layers are no longer shaded. The game sets the
setting from `android_cutout_depth_prepass` and adds `depth_prepass_alpha` to the cut-out builds it chooses.
RenderingDevice now accepts a fragment stage that leaves out a colour attachment whose writes the blend state
masks off entirely (the depth-only version in the colour pass); every pipeline it accepted before is unchanged.
The depth draws are added to the viewport's draw-call count (Mobile otherwise reports its visible instances there),
and a `[cutout-prepass]` line every 10 s logs how many views drew a pre-pass and how many depth draws they had.

